The function `PriorIndexOf` is used to find the index of the first occurrence of a specified value in a given vector. It is a part of the `RH.ModelSerializer` class, which is used for serializing and deserializing data.

Here is an example of how to use `PriorIndexOf`:

```c
#include <RH.ModelSerializer.h>

using namespace RH;

int main() {
    // Create a vector
    vector<int> vec = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};

    // Find the index of the first occurrence of 3
    int index = PriorIndexOf(vec, 3);

    // Check if the index is valid
    if (index!= -1) {
        std::cout << "3 is present in the vector" << std::endl;
    } else {
        std::cout << "3 is not present in the vector" << std::endl;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

